{"id":"mahabharata-7-003","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":3,"title":"तृतीयोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 3 · Karna's vow","summary":{"en":"Karna laments over Bhishma on his bed of arrows and tells him that now he himself, Bhishma's blessed child, will fight. He vows to defeat Arjuna and the Pandavas.","kn":"ಬಾಣಶಯ್ಯೆಯಲ್ಲಿರುವ ಭೀಷ್ಮನ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಕರ್ಣ ದುಃಖಿಸಿ, ಇನ್ನು ತಾನೇ ಹೋರಾಡುವೆನೆಂದು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನ ಮತ್ತು ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ಸೋಲಿಸುವೆನೆಂದು ಪ್ರತಿಜ್ಞೆ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"बाणशय्या पर लेटे भीष्म के लिए कर्ण शोक करता है और कहता है कि अब वह स्वयं लड़ेगा। वह अर्जुन और पाण्डवों को हराने की प्रतिज्ञा करता है।","te":"బాణశయ్యపై ఉన్న భీష్ముని కోసం కర్ణుడు దుఃఖించి ఇకపై తానే పోరాడతానని అంటాడు. అర్జునుని, పాండవులను జయిస్తానని ప్రతిజ్ఞ చేస్తాడు.","ta":"அம்புப் படுக்கையிலுள்ள பீஷ்மருக்காகக் கர்ணன் வருந்தி, இனி தானே போரிடுவதாகக் கூறுகிறான். அர்ஜுனனையும் பாண்டவரையும் வெல்வதாகச் சபதம் செய்கிறான்.","ml":"അമ്പുകളുടെ ശയ്യയിൽ കിടക്കുന്ന ഭീഷ്മരെക്കുറിച്ച് കർണ്ണൻ വിലപിക്കുന്നു; ഭീഷ്മരുടെ അനുഗൃഹീത പുത്രനായ താൻ ഇനി യുദ്ധം ചെയ്യുമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. അർജുനനെയും പാണ്ഡവരെയും തോൽപ്പിക്കുമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പ്രതിജ്ഞയെടുക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.3; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"द्रोणाभिषेकपर्व","titleEn":"Dronabhisheka Parva (Drona's consecration)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"शरतल्पे महात्मानं शयानममितौजसम् ।\nमहावातसमूहेन समुद्रमिव शोषितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-souled Bhishma of boundless energy lay on his bed of arrows, like an ocean dried up by a great mass of storm winds."}},{"n":2,"text":"दिव्यैरस्त्रैर्महेष्वासं पातितं सव्यसाचिना ।\nजयाशां तव पुत्राणां संभग्नां शर्म वर्म च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty archer had been felled by the left-handed archer, Arjuna, with divine weapons, and with him the hope of victory for your sons, their refuge and their armor, was shattered."}},{"n":3,"text":"अपाराणामिव द्वीपमगाधे गाधमिच्छताम् ।\nस्रोतसा यामुनेनेव शरौघेण परिप्लुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was like an island to those without a shore in unfathomable waters who seek a shallow place, now flooded by a torrent of arrows like the current of the Yamuna."}},{"n":4,"text":"महान्तमिव मैनाकमसह्यं भुवि पातितम् ।\nनभश्च्युतमिवादित्यं पतितं धरणीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was like the great Mount Mainaka, unassailable, thrown down upon the earth, or like the sun fallen from the sky onto the ground."}},{"n":5,"text":"शतक्रतोरिवाचिन्त्यं पुरा वृत्रेण निर्जयम् ।\nमोहनं सर्वसैन्यस्य युधि भीष्मस्य पातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fall of Bhishma in battle, which bewildered the whole army, was as unthinkable as Indra's earlier defeat at the hands of Vritra."}},{"n":6,"text":"ककुदं सर्वसैन्यानां लक्ष्म सर्वधनुष्मताम् ।\nधनंजयशरव्याप्तं पितरं ते महाव्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was the high hump of all armies, the emblem of all archers, your father of great vows, covered with Dhananjaya's arrows."}},{"n":7,"text":"तं वीरशयने वीरं शयानं पुरुषर्षभम् ।\nभीष्ममाधिरथिर्दृष्ट्वा भरतानाममध्यमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that tiger among men, the hero Bhishma, best of the Bharatas, lying on his hero's bed, Radha's son Karna, son of Adhiratha, was distressed."}},{"n":8,"text":"अवतीर्य रथादार्तो बाष्पव्याकुलिताक्षरम् ।\nअभिवाद्याञ्जलिं बद्ध्वा वन्दमानोऽभ्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He got down from his chariot, his voice choked with tears, greeted Bhishma, joined his palms, and bowing spoke."}},{"n":9,"text":"कर्णोऽहमस्मि भद्रं ते अद्य मा वद भारत ।\nपुण्यया क्षेमया वाचा चक्षुषा चावलोकय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am Karna, may good fortune be yours. Speak to me today, O Bharata. Look at me with an auspicious, kindly word and glance."}},{"n":10,"text":"न नूनं सुकृतस्येह फलं कश्चित्समश्नुते ।\nयत्र धर्मपरो वृद्धः शेते भुवि भवानिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely no one here enjoys the fruit of good deeds, since you, an elder devoted to dharma, lie here on the ground."}},{"n":11,"text":"कोशसंजनने मन्त्रे व्यूहप्रहरणेषु च ।\nनाथमन्यं न पश्यामि कुरूणां कुरुसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"In managing the treasury, in counsel, in battle arrays and in striking with weapons, I see no other protector for the Kurus, best of the Kurus."}},{"n":12,"text":"बुद्ध्या विशुद्धया युक्तो यः कुरूंस्तारयेद्भयात् ।\nयोधांस्त्वमप्लवे हित्वा पितृलोकं गमिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, gifted with pure wisdom, who would carry the Kurus across danger, have left the warriors without a raft and will go to the world of the ancestors."}},{"n":13,"text":"अद्य प्रभृति संक्रुद्धा व्याघ्रा इव मृगक्षयम् ।\nपाण्डवा भरतश्रेष्ठ करिष्यन्ति कुरुक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From today the Pandavas, enraged, will bring about the Kuru destruction, best of the Bharatas, as tigers destroy herds of deer."}},{"n":14,"text":"अद्य गाण्डीवघोषस्य वीर्यज्ञाः सव्यसाचिनः ।\nकुरवः संत्रसिष्यन्ति वज्रपाणेरिवासुराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today the Kurus, who know the might of Arjuna, the left-handed archer, and the twang of the Gandiva, will tremble, as the asuras did before the wielder of the thunderbolt."}},{"n":15,"text":"अद्य गाण्डीवमुक्तानामशनीनामिव स्वनः ।\nत्रासयिष्यति संग्रामे कुरूनन्यांश्च पार्थिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today the sound of the arrows loosed from the Gandiva, like thunderbolts, will terrify the Kurus and the other kings in battle."}},{"n":16,"text":"समिद्धोऽग्निर्यथा वीर महाज्वालो द्रुमान्दहेत् ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रान्प्रधक्ष्यन्ति तथा बाणाः किरीटिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a kindled fire with great flames burns trees, O hero, so the arrows of the diademed Arjuna will burn up the sons of Dhritarashtra."}},{"n":17,"text":"येन येन प्रसरतो वाय्वग्नी सहितौ वने ।\nतेन तेन प्रदहतो भगवन्तौ यदिच्छतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wherever wind and fire together spread through a forest, they burn, those two lords, as they wish."}},{"n":18,"text":"यादृशोऽग्निः समिद्धो हि तादृक्पार्थो न संशयः ।\nयथा वायुर्नरव्याघ्र तथा कृष्णो न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna is like a kindled fire, no doubt, and Krishna is like the wind, tiger among men, no doubt."}},{"n":19,"text":"नदतः पाञ्चजन्यस्य रसतो गाण्डिवस्य च ।\nश्रुत्वा सर्वाणि सैन्यानि त्रासं यास्यन्ति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the roar of the Panchajanya and the thunder of the Gandiva, all the armies will be seized with terror, O Bharata."}},{"n":20,"text":"कपिध्वजस्य चोत्पाते रथस्यामित्रकर्शिनः ।\nशब्दं सोढुं न शक्ष्यन्ति त्वामृते वीर पार्थिवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kings, O hero, will not be able to bear the sound of the monkey-bannered chariot of that destroyer of foes as it charges, without you."}},{"n":21,"text":"को ह्यर्जुनं रणे योद्धुं त्वदन्यः पार्थिवोऽर्हति ।\nयस्य दिव्यानि कर्माणि प्रवदन्ति मनीषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who other than you, among kings, is fit to fight Arjuna in battle, whose divine deeds the wise proclaim?"}},{"n":22,"text":"अमानुषश्च संग्रामस्त्र्यम्बकेन च धीमतः ।\nतस्माच्चैव वरः प्राप्तो दुष्प्रापश्चाकृतात्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His battle with the three-eyed god was beyond human, and from him that wise man received a boon hard for those of unrefined soul to obtain."}},{"n":23,"text":"तमद्याहं पाण्डवं युद्धशौण्ड-\nममृष्यमाणो भवतानुशिष्टः ।\nआशीविषं दृष्टिहरं सुघोर-\nमियां पुरस्कृत्य वधं जयं वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today, unable to endure it, and instructed by you, I will go against that Pandava, skilled in battle, venomous-eyed and most terrible, aiming at either his death or victory.\""}}]}]}